      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "Preseason can be a cruel sorting machine, and Toronto is using it that way - by trimming the fat and testing who can survive the first real squeeze. <strong>Steven Lorentz cleared waivers after the Leafs sent eight players down</strong>, a tidy little bit of roster housekeeping that tells you camp has moved from experimentation to judgment. The exhibition wins over Ottawa - 6-1 and 4-2 - looked sharp enough, while the split-squad losses to Montreal reminded everyone this is still a roster under construction, not a finished product. The bigger story now is integration: new faces, new combinations, and a lineup that still has a few names fighting for oxygen. The Leafs open Tuesday night against Montreal, and that matters. <strong>What happens between now and puck drop will decide who gets to dress when the games count for real.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
