      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "Training camp has a way of stripping the varnish off a roster, and in Toronto the shine is all on Scottie Barnes. <strong>That's the headline now: he is the linchpin, the fulcrum, the piece everything else has to orbit</strong> - from Darko Rajakovic's lineups to whatever role Kawhi Leonard's return to the franchise's story truly settles into. The Raptors open preseason Saturday against Miami, but the real test arrives long before the tipoff at 7:00 p.m. ET: who claims the minutes behind Barnes, who sticks in the rotation, and who gets squeezed out when the regular season begins Oct. 21 against Chicago. This is a team still drawing its map. <strong>Watch the guard rotation and the frontcourt pecking order in camp - those battles will tell you more than any exhibition score.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
